{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The five kings of Midian.</b> But do I not see that Scripture lists five? Why was it necessary to say 'five'? Rather, to teach you that they were all equal in counsel and were all equal in punishment (there); Balaam went there to take his wage for the twenty-four thousand he caused to fall from Israel by his counsel, and he went forth from Midian to meet Israel and to urge an evil plan — he said to them: When you were sixty myriad you could not prevail against them, and now twelve thousand of you come to do battle? They paid him his wage in full and did not cheat him (Sifrei)." "<b>With the sword.</b> He came against Israel and exchanged his craft for their craft — for they prevail only with their mouths and through prayer and supplication. He came and seized their craft to curse them with his mouth; so they too came against him and exchanged their craft for the craft of the nations, who come with the sword, as it says: ״וְעַל חַרְבְּךָ תִּחְיֶה״ (Genesis 27)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:23.412341712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}